{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_clients", "label": "Clients (docs/clients.md)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/clients.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_clients_server_client_model", "label": "One server, everything else is a client", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/clients.md", "source_location": "intro", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One machine runs the models, holds the tokens and answers; every other microphone sends what it hears and plays what it is sent, running no models. The server's own microphone is one client among these with no special privileges."}, {"id": "docs_clients_parlour_token", "label": "PARLOUR_TOKEN and loopback-only default", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/clients.md", "source_location": "## The token", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Without a token the server only listens on loopback and does not advertise, because a voice assistant on an open port can turn the heating on and read your shopping list. A browser on the same machine addressed by a name other than localhost counts as somewhere else. Token is sent as Authorization: Bearer or ?token= for the socket and phone page; secrets set reads from stdin so it never lands in shell history."}, {"id": "docs_clients_satellite", "label": "Satellite role", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/clients.md", "source_location": "## A satellite", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Any Mac with Node, ffmpeg and the parlour package; no models, keys or GPU. It finds the server by Bonjour once and pins the address in serverUrl thereafter, because anything on the network can advertise _parlour._tcp and the satellite hands its token to whatever it connects to, so the first server it trusts is the only one it trusts. Backs off up to satellite.retryMs when the server is down. Plays the server's speech so the voice is the same in every room."}, {"id": "docs_clients_local_wake", "label": "satellite.localWake", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/clients.md", "source_location": "## A satellite", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Runs the wake word on the satellite and streams only what follows; costs a copy of the models on that machine and saves a constant 32 KB/s. Off by default because it is one less thing to keep in step."}, {"id": "docs_clients_phone_page", "label": "Phone push-to-talk page (/ and POST /voice)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/clients.md", "source_location": "## A phone", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Posts one recording to POST /voice?client=phone&room=kitchen and gets { heard, reply, via, audio } with a base64 WAV. A ?token=...&room= link fills in settings so nothing is typed on a phone keyboard. Safari only grants microphone over HTTPS or localhost, so iOS needs a reverse proxy or Tailscale."}, {"id": "docs_clients_listen_websocket", "label": "/listen WebSocket (wake mode and push mode)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/clients.md", "source_location": "## Custom hardware", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Send 16 kHz mono s16 PCM in binary frames of any size; the server re-cuts to 80 ms frames. Wake mode runs the server's own openWakeWord and endpointing so hardware can be just a mic, speaker and network stack. Push mode (&mode=push) uses start/end/cancel messages for a button or hardware with its own wake word. {type:spoke} lets the server resume listening immediately after playback."}, {"id": "docs_clients_ask_endpoint", "label": "POST /ask for automations", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/clients.md", "source_location": "## Automations and scripts", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "JSON content type is required because a web form can post text/plain anywhere without the browser asking first but cannot claim to be JSON (CSRF defence). Returns { reply, via }; callers without a client id share the api session."}, {"id": "docs_clients_health_endpoint", "label": "GET /health (no token)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/clients.md", "source_location": "## The token", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_clients_bonjour_discovery", "label": "Bonjour advertisement _parlour._tcp", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/clients.md", "source_location": "## Bonjour", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "TXT record says role=server, token=required|none, api=/v1. Name is discovery.name or '<config.name> on <hostname>'. discovery.enabled false means every satellite needs serverUrl filled in."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_clients", "target": "docs_home_assistant", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/clients.md", "source_location": "## Home Assistant, and the satellites you already have", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_clients_server_client_model", "target": "docs_architecture_per_client_session", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/clients.md", "source_location": "intro", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_clients_server_client_model", "target": "docs_clients_bonjour_discovery", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/clients.md", "source_location": "intro", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_clients_parlour_token", "target": "docs_clients_bonjour_discovery", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/clients.md", "source_location": "## The token", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_clients_parlour_token", "target": "docs_architecture_secrets_env", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/clients.md", "source_location": "## The token", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_clients_parlour_token", "target": "docs_architecture_doctor", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/clients.md", "source_location": "## The token", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_clients_satellite", "target": "docs_clients_bonjour_discovery", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/clients.md", "source_location": "## A satellite", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_clients_satellite", "target": "docs_clients_parlour_token", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/clients.md", "source_location": "## A satellite", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_clients_satellite", "target": "docs_clients_local_wake", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/clients.md", "source_location": "## A satellite", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_clients_satellite", "target": "docs_clients_listen_websocket", "relation": "references", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "docs/clients.md", "source_location": "## A satellite", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_clients_local_wake", "target": "docs_architecture_openwakeword", "relation": "references", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/clients.md", "source_location": "## A satellite", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_clients_phone_page", "target": "docs_clients_parlour_token", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/clients.md", "source_location": "## A phone", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_clients_phone_page", "target": "packages_parlour_src_server_web_index", "relation": "references", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/clients.md", "source_location": "## A phone", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_clients_listen_websocket", "target": "docs_architecture_voice_session_state_machine", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/clients.md", "source_location": "## Custom hardware", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_clients_listen_websocket", "target": "docs_architecture_openwakeword", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/clients.md", "source_location": "## Custom hardware", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_clients_listen_websocket", "target": "docs_architecture_endpointer", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/clients.md", "source_location": "## Custom hardware", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_clients_ask_endpoint", "target": "docs_clients_parlour_token", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/clients.md", "source_location": "## Automations and scripts", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_clients_ask_endpoint", "target": "docs_architecture_per_client_session", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/clients.md", "source_location": "## Automations and scripts", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_clients_health_endpoint", "target": "docs_architecture_buildagent", "relation": "references", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.75, "source_file": "docs/clients.md", "source_location": "## The token (tools count, cloud)", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_clients_bonjour_discovery", "target": "docs_architecture_paths", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/clients.md", "source_location": "## Bonjour", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_clients_phone_page", "target": "docs_clients_listen_websocket", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.75, "source_file": "docs/clients.md", "source_location": "## A phone / ## Custom hardware", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_clients_ask_endpoint", "target": "docs_home_assistant_openai_conversation", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.75, "source_file": "docs/clients.md", "source_location": "## Automations and scripts", "weight": 1.0}], "hyperedges": [{"id": "parlour_client_kinds", "label": "Every kind of Parlour client sharing one server, one token and per-client sessions", "nodes": ["docs_clients_satellite", "docs_clients_phone_page", "docs_clients_listen_websocket", "docs_clients_ask_endpoint", "docs_home_assistant_openai_conversation", "docs_clients_parlour_token", "docs_architecture_per_client_session"], "relation": "participate_in", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/clients.md"}]}